# Scope-specific routing only: some developers set npmmirror as their *global*
# default registry, and it has not synced the latest of this scope, so pin it to
# the official registry. The default `registry` and `store-dir` are intentionally
# NOT set here — they are machine/region specific and belong in each developer's
# global ~/.npmrc. Committing them breaks Linux/macOS (the `E:\...` store path is
# treated as a literal directory name) and silently redirects `pnpm publish`
# away from registry.npmjs.org, defeating OIDC Trusted Publishing.
@maxim_mazurok:registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
